sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Admin as Device Admin
    participant UI as Admin UI
    participant API as DevicesController
    participant Service as DeviceService
    participant DB as Gateway Database
    participant Device as Medical Device
    participant EST as EstController
    participant Orch as EnrollmentOrchestrator
    participant Notify as NotificationDispatcher
    participant Revoker as Future Gateway Revocation Service
    participant Factory as CaConnectorFactory
    participant CA as CA Backend

    Admin->>UI: Remove device trust
    UI->>API: POST /api/devices/{id}/remove
    API->>Service: RemoveAsync(id)
    Service->>DB: Load device
    DB-->>Service: Device
    Service->>Service: Set Status = Removed and RemovedAt = now
    Service->>DB: Save device
    Service-->>API: DeviceDto(status=removed)
    API-->>UI: 200 OK
    UI-->>Admin: Device removed from gateway trust

    Note over Service,CA: Current admin API does not call ICaConnector.RevokeCertificateAsync or mark existing certificates revoked.

    Device->>EST: Later POST /.well-known/est/simplereenroll with old client cert
    EST->>Orch: ReenrollAsync(profileId, csr, oldCert, clientIp)
    Orch->>DB: Resolve stored certificate and device
    DB-->>Orch: Certificate maps to removed device
    Orch->>Orch: Reject because device is not active
    Orch->>Notify: NotifyEnrollmentRejectedAsync
    Notify-->>Orch: Notification attempted if enabled
    Orch-->>EST: Failed("Device is not active", 403)
    EST-->>Device: 403 JSON error

    opt Future direct CA-side certificate revocation
        Admin->>UI: Revoke certificate serial
        UI->>Revoker: Request revoke(serial, reason)
        Revoker->>DB: Load certificate and active or owning backend
        DB-->>Revoker: Certificate and CA backend
        Revoker->>Factory: CreateConnector(backend)
        Factory-->>Revoker: ICaConnector
        Revoker->>CA: RevokeCertificateAsync(serial, reason)
        alt Connector and CA support revocation
            CA-->>Revoker: true
            Revoker->>DB: Set Certificate.Status = Revoked
            Revoker-->>UI: Revoked
        else Connector does not support revocation
            CA-->>Revoker: false
            Revoker-->>UI: Revocation unavailable; trust removal still blocks renewals
        end
    end
